# Yanchan — what does NOT belong in the repository.
#
# The rule behind every line here: if a machine can regenerate it, or if it is
# video, it stays out. What is kept is the code, the two scripts, the dependency
# list, and the small JSON files that are the pipeline's store of record.
#
# Sizes measured on the build machine, for scale:
#   streams/                24 GB     raw captures + proxies
#   *.mp4 in the repo root   8 GB     three VODs
#   tools/clip-pipeline/work 1.6 GB   extracted audio, music maps, previews
#   tools/clip-pipeline/.venv 1.0 GB  rebuildable with ./install.sh
#   clips/                 491 MB     rendered clips
#   site/node_modules      (large)    rebuildable with ./install.sh


# --- Installed dependencies -----------------------------------------------
# Both are rebuilt by ./install.sh. The venv especially MUST NOT be committed:
# it hard-codes absolute paths to the machine that created it, so a copy is
# broken on arrival anywhere else. That is the whole reason requirements.txt
# exists.
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.Python
pip-wheel-metadata/


# --- Build output ----------------------------------------------------------
.next/
out/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.vercel/


# --- Source video ----------------------------------------------------------
# A single Kick VOD is about 2.8 GB. Captures live in streams/, and downloads
# land in the repo root (fetch_vod.py --output-dir defaults there).
/*.mp4
/*.mkv
/*.webm
/*.mov
/*.ts


# --- streams/ — captures, proxies and per-stream state ---------------------
# 24 GB of video, but streams/archive.json is the archive of record: it is what
# knows which stream exists, which was captured, and which Kick has already
# deleted. Small, hand-corrected, and irreplaceable — so it is kept.
/streams/*
!/streams/archive.json
!/streams/waveform/
/streams/waveform/*
!/streams/waveform/*.json
!/streams/prepare/
/streams/prepare/*
!/streams/prepare/*.json


# --- clips/ — rendered output, and the library that describes it -----------
# The rendered MP4s are regenerable from the library plus the source VOD, so
# they go. clips/library.json does NOT: it holds every clip's in/out points,
# hand-written hooks, approval status and edit history. It is the store of
# record, it is 44 KB, and losing it loses the human work. Same for the framing
# locks and the selection settings.
/clips/*
!/clips/library.json
!/clips/framing-locks.json
!/clips/selection-settings.json
!/clips/strategy.md


# --- Intermediate work -----------------------------------------------------
# Per-stream extracted audio (WAV), previews and draft renders. All regenerated
# by prepare_stream.py.
# EXCEPTION — this handoff repo ships two small state files per stream dir,
# music.json and calibration.json, so the timeline and editor views render
# 1:1 on a fresh clone. Everything else in work/ still stays out.
/tools/clip-pipeline/work/*
!/tools/clip-pipeline/work/*/
/tools/clip-pipeline/work/*/*
!/tools/clip-pipeline/work/*/*.json


# --- Model caches ----------------------------------------------------------
# Whisper's speech models. The default 'small' is ~480 MB and 'medium' is 1.5 GB.
# They download themselves on first use; the real cache is ~/.cache/whisper,
# outside the repo, and these patterns catch any copy that lands inside it.
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.tflite
.cache/
whisper_cache/
/tools/clip-pipeline/models/


# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem


# --- macOS and editor noise ------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/


# --- site/ — the dashboard is a normal directory in this repo ---------------
# It carries its own ignore rules via the entries above (node_modules, .next,
# .vercel). In the upstream working repo site/ was a nested git repository;
# here it is plain source and must be tracked.


# --- Design and business material, not the program -------------------------
# This repo's working folder holds ~640 MB of binaries that belong to other
# lanes: pitch decks, merch artwork, marketing imagery, generated stills,
# wireframes. None of it is the YP Digital Dash, none of it is regenerated by
# anything here, and git is a poor place to keep large binaries — once committed
# they sit in history forever, in every clone.
#
# NOTHING IS DELETED BY THIS. Every file stays exactly where it is on disk; it
# is simply not tracked. If any of it should be versioned, it wants its own repo
# (or Drive), not this one.
/Yanchan-Produced/
/merch/
/yanchanproduced-com-assets/
/extracted-assets/
/wireframes/
/*.jpg
/*.JPG
/*.jpeg
/*.png
/*.webp
/*.pdf
/*.ai
/*.eps
/*.zip
/*.docx
/*.excalidraw

# Tool scratch.
/.playwright-mcp/


# --- Deliberately NOT ignored ----------------------------------------------
# Spelled out because they look like build artefacts and are not:
#   tools/clip-pipeline/requirements.txt   the only description of what to install
#   tools/clip-pipeline/doctor.py          preflight check
#   tools/clip-pipeline/assets/*.png       watermark and logo burned into renders
#   install.sh, start.sh                   how anyone else gets this running
#   clips/library.json                     the store of record (see above)
#   streams/archive.json                   the stream archive (see above)
!/tools/clip-pipeline/requirements.txt
!/tools/clip-pipeline/assets/
